00:00:20.319 --> 00:00:21.920
-It's beautiful.
-Yeah.

00:00:21.920 --> 00:00:25.491
-But you know, it was really --
I got presented the idea

00:00:25.491 --> 00:00:28.628
to play the genie in "Aladdin,"

00:00:28.628 --> 00:00:30.963
you know, and the first thing
is, "Hell no."

00:00:30.963 --> 00:00:32.699
You know, it's like, you know,

00:00:32.699 --> 00:00:36.302
when Robin Williams
smashed that role, you know.

00:00:36.302 --> 00:00:38.037
And it's like, when you look at
things like that,

00:00:38.037 --> 00:00:41.040
you always try to find, like,
what would you do differently?

00:00:41.040 --> 00:00:43.342
What would you add to that?

00:00:43.342 --> 00:00:45.578
So I looked at it
and the first thing was,

00:00:45.578 --> 00:00:47.747
I didn't feel like
I wanted to touch it.

00:00:47.747 --> 00:00:51.050
But then I spent some time with
it, and, you know,

00:00:51.050 --> 00:00:52.985
I met with the directors
and talked about it.

00:00:52.985 --> 00:00:54.921
-I think you're perfect.
-Oh, thank you, man.

00:00:54.921 --> 00:00:56.588
-I think you're perfect
for the role.

00:00:56.588 --> 00:00:58.757
Absolutely a great decision.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:58.757 --> 00:00:59.658
Phenomenal, man.
-Thank you.

00:00:59.658 --> 00:01:01.027
Quest will know this.

00:01:01.027 --> 00:01:05.031
What did it for me, when I was
messing with the music,

00:01:05.031 --> 00:01:06.665
